HST Office: gtk3 clipboard queries off the main thread are made on the main thread.

An office driven over UNO hung for good (Linux, gtk3) while a mode switch or a document load ran on the UNO
request thread and built a Paste control (menubar, toolbar or ribbon): its first state asks the system
clipboard (SwBaseShell::StateClpbrd -> TransferableDataHelper::CreateFromSystemClipboard ->
GtkClipboardTransferable::getTransferDataFlavorsAsVector -> gtk_clipboard_wait_for_targets ->
g_main_loop_run). That nested loop runs the default glib main context on the request thread; the main thread
then waits for the context in g_main_context_iteration (g_cond_wait), the selection reply is never
dispatched and neither thread moves again. gdb stacks of 4 hangs of tests/runtime/check-ui-mode-cycle-stress.py
(after 0 to 19 rounds) all show this. A user's clicks run on the main thread and never met it.

GtkClipboardTransferable::getTransferData and getTransferDataFlavorsAsVector now run on the main thread when
called from another one (vcl::solarthread::syncExecute, which releases the SolarMutex while it waits), so
gtk_clipboard_wait_* only ever runs on the main thread.

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).

--- a/vcl/unx/gtk3/gtkinst.cxx
+++ b/vcl/unx/gtk3/gtkinst.cxx
@@ -81,6 +81,8 @@
 
 #include <basegfx/numeric/ftools.hxx>
 #include <vcl/settings.hxx>
+#include <vcl/svapp.hxx>
+#include <vcl/threadex.hxx>
 
 #include <dlfcn.h>
 #include <fcntl.h>
@@ -891,6 +893,15 @@
 
     virtual css::uno::Any SAL_CALL getTransferData(const css::datatransfer::DataFlavor& rFlavor) override
     {
+        // HST: gtk_clipboard_wait_* runs a nested loop of the default main context. Called off the main thread
+        // (a UNO client's request: a Paste state while a toolbar, menubar or ribbon is built) that thread takes the
+        // context while the main thread waits for it, and both wait for good. Ask from the main thread instead.
+        if (!Application::IsMainThread())
+        {
+            SolarMutexGuard aGuard; // syncExecute releases it (all levels) while the main thread runs the query
+            return vcl::solarthread::syncExecute([this, &rFlavor]() { return getTransferData(rFlavor); });
+        }
+
         css::uno::Any aRet;
 
         css::datatransfer::DataFlavor aFlavor(rFlavor);
@@ -953,6 +964,12 @@
     std::vector<css::datatransfer::DataFlavor> getTransferDataFlavorsAsVector()
         override
     {
+        if (!Application::IsMainThread()) // HST: see getTransferData
+        {
+            SolarMutexGuard aGuard;
+            return vcl::solarthread::syncExecute([this]() { return getTransferDataFlavorsAsVector(); });
+        }
+
         std::vector<css::datatransfer::DataFlavor> aVector;
 
         GdkClipboard* clipboard = clipboard_get(m_eSelection);
